<title>USA: U.S. Bancorp files $1.0 bln shelf debt.</title>
<headline>U.S. Bancorp files $1.0 bln shelf debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Bancorp filed Thursday with the Securities and Exchange Commission up to $1.0 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, including investments in or extensions of credit to existing and future subsidiaries, potential acquisitions ofother baning and financial services businesses, repurchase of outstanding common stock and repayment of borrowings.</p>
<p>No underwriters were listed in the filing.</p>
